#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179531 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179675 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3be2c44e-775f-53fa-a078-cff25eaea903" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Sum of Line Integrals With Respect to X and Y"}] :question/id #uuid "7cec344e-596a-51ce-87cc-d0e44dc48df4" :question/math-academy-id "e-7118" :question/problem "Construct a definite integral that is equivalent to $\\displaystyle \\int\\limits_C (x^2+y)\\,\\mathrm{d}x + x\\,\\mathrm{d}y,$ where $C$ is parametrized by $\\mathbf{r}(t) = t\\,\\mathbf{i} + t^2\\,\\mathbf{j}$ for $t\\in\\left[0,1\\right].$" :question/worked-solution "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t) = t, \\qquad\ny(t) = t^2.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $\\mathbf r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =i+2t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}({x}^{2}+y)\\,dx+x\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+y)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(({x}^{2}+y)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({t}^{2}+{t}^{2})\\cdot 1+t\\cdot 2t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{t}^{2}+2{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{1}{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179591 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179729 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b5ecc45-95ec-55c0-86bf-bbaeffef4049" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Sum of Line Integrals With Respect to X, Y, and Z"}] :question/id #uuid "2b0b2d1f-df55-56cf-9ae9-ccef499e2352" :question/math-academy-id "e-9517" :question/problem "Construct a definite integral that is equivalent to $\\displaystyle \\int\\limits_C x^3\\,\\mathrm{d}x + z\\,\\mathrm{d}y + y\\,\\mathrm{d}z,$ where $C$ is a portion of the helix $\\mathbf{r}(t)=2t\\,\\mathbf{i} + \\cos t\\,\\mathbf{j} + \\sin t\\,\\mathbf{k}$ for $t\\in[0,\\pi]?$" :question/worked-solution "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t) =2t, \\qquad \ny(t) = \\cos t , \\qquad \nz(t) = \\sin t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $\\mathbf r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,k \\\\  & =2\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}{x}^{3}\\,dx+z\\,dy+y\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{x}^{3}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+z\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+y\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }({x}^{3}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+z\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+y\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2t)^{3}\\cdot (2)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }16{t}^{3}-{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }16{t}^{3}+({cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t)\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }16{t}^{3}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,dt\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179596 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179734 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2daf57e1-a02d-5e5f-b4a4-bb8ae9638a75" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Line Integral"}] :question/id #uuid "c18fbc4a-24d5-517d-9a3c-949a11787076" :question/math-academy-id "e-9528" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int\\limits_C y\\,\\mathrm{d}x -x\\,\\mathrm{d}y ,$ where $C$ is a portion of the ellipse parametrized by $\\mathbf{r}(t)=\\cos t\\,\\mathbf{i} + 3\\sin t\\,\\mathbf{j}$ for $t\\in[0,\\pi].$" :question/worked-solution "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t) = \\cos t, \\qquad\ny(t) = 3\\sin t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $\\mathbf r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}y\\,dx-x\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt-x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\cdot 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }-3{sin}^{2}⁡t-3{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,dt \\\\  & =-3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,dt \\\\  & =-3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\,dt \\\\  & =-3{t|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-3\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259723 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179734 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2daf57e1-a02d-5e5f-b4a4-bb8ae9638a75" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Line Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43316bd7-4a4d-5b4e-a6f6-c7ace880dd8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60{\\pi }^{2}-12\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257374} {:answer/id #uuid "4cb62704-b7aa-5926-aa39-7feb9b27a9a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36{\\pi }^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257444} {:answer/id #uuid "964aceea-63a4-5f26-8e5f-5f425c3c618a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72{\\pi }^{4}-18\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258106} {:answer/id #uuid "a1a4e628-b297-5247-9399-119c459a3598" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24{\\pi }^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258198} {:answer/id #uuid "ede44b18-3839-5b15-8555-09a33587c56a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13{\\pi }^{2}+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258840}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "964aceea-63a4-5f26-8e5f-5f425c3c618a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72{\\pi }^{4}-18\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258106} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ccf2aea-2200-59cd-b324-9c5869c62e7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259220}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8cf6c777-07aa-500d-afdd-abfd78e3d9eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-124712" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}x\\,dx-z\\,dy+y\\,dz,$ where $C$ is a portion of the curve $r(t)=3{t}^{2}\\,i+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ].$" :question/worked-solution "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=3{t}^{2},\\,y(t)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,z(t)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,k \\\\  & =6t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}x\\,dx-z\\,dy+y\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt-z\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+y\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-z\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+y\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }3{t}^{2}\\cdot (6t)-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot (3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot (-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }18{t}^{3}-9{cos}^{2}⁡t-9{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }18{t}^{3}-9\\,dt \\\\  & =(\\frac{9{t}^{4}}{2}-9t){|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =72{\\pi }^{4}-18\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387574 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179729 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b5ecc45-95ec-55c0-86bf-bbaeffef4049" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Sum of Line Integrals With Respect to X, Y, and Z"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ccc6fb9f-9d2e-586c-9834-4e0c109c42ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{t}^{3}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387576} {:answer/id #uuid "247499a3-ebb9-55e0-b9af-0357640b07f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{t}^{2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387577} {:answer/id #uuid "3c6fa0df-443b-518b-9a95-9f92c40c9da3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡t+1\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387578} {:answer/id #uuid "f7ddcaf6-928b-502d-b5d2-f9a85dfa535e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{3}⁡t\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387579} {:answer/id #uuid "d5a87944-33b0-54c6-917e-0f0893016a58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387580}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ccc6fb9f-9d2e-586c-9834-4e0c109c42ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{t}^{3}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387576} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff5936f7-aee3-5c0d-8970-fd47f2c8c007" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387575}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fb7ae2bd-0784-56ff-b58a-eea210c6700b" :question/math-academy-id "q-124809" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}{x}^{3}\\,dx+z\\,dy+y\\,dz,$ where $C$ is a portion of the helix $r(t)=t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,\\pi ]?$" :question/worked-solution "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=t,\\,y(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,z(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,k \\\\  & =\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}{x}^{3}\\,dx+z\\,dy+y\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{x}^{3}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+z\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+y\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }({x}^{3}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+z\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+y\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{t}^{3}\\cdot (1)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{t}^{3}+{cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{t}^{3}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,dt\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259741 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179729 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b5ecc45-95ec-55c0-86bf-bbaeffef4049" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Sum of Line Integrals With Respect to X, Y, and Z"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b352b54-a7f8-546e-9f00-4b5bfb33c5f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}2{t}^{4}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257012} {:answer/id #uuid "1c2ced42-6a95-5c97-90e2-6beb9ad77a0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}2{t}^{3}+{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257016} {:answer/id #uuid "27e3b23c-ddba-547d-b104-e9c956beb181" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}2{t}^{3}+2\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257136} {:answer/id #uuid "2b242858-e2f0-5eae-a779-11c5785191a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}2{t}^{4}-2{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257164} {:answer/id #uuid "fe92af0d-aea8-5f4a-a30a-92f2201678ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}2{t}^{5}-4\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259016}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe92af0d-aea8-5f4a-a30a-92f2201678ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}2{t}^{5}-4\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259016} :answer-field/id #uuid "150d4e70-9211-5bfc-b576-a7ee0524c4ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259070}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b989f90c-82b4-5851-b56d-21f399df4340" :question/math-academy-id "q-124830" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}-y\\,dx+x\\,dy+{z}^{2}\\,dz,$ where $C$ is a portion of the curve $r(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+{t}^{2}\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]?$" :question/worked-solution "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y(t)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,z(t)={t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+2t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}-y\\,dx+x\\,dy+{z}^{2}\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}-y\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+{z}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}(-y\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+{z}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)+{t}^{4}\\cdot (2t)\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}2{t}^{5}-4{sin}^{2}⁡t-4{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}2{t}^{5}-4\\,dt\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259742 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179729 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b5ecc45-95ec-55c0-86bf-bbaeffef4049" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Sum of Line Integrals With Respect to X, Y, and Z"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07c746cb-15fe-5580-b062-0c07c2a5993a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}t+2\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256848} {:answer/id #uuid "088fc215-12ab-5eaf-a1a6-04368e4d0bde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}{t}^{2}+9\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256855} {:answer/id #uuid "27b7f8a2-50cc-5b37-b671-bd2c4ecd85e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257134} {:answer/id #uuid "a2423930-a3be-53c6-859c-e912a0d06dcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}{t}^{2}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258201} {:answer/id #uuid "c9e75376-217c-5d7c-bab3-f0e6a6c862eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}{t}^{2}+{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258540}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07c746cb-15fe-5580-b062-0c07c2a5993a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}t+2\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256848} :answer-field/id #uuid "169be3a6-1bf9-557b-99a4-c4fa43ec6ab1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259072}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f06cbe05-4a7e-555b-8b18-98e969a7aace" :question/math-academy-id "q-124832" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}-y\\,dx+x\\,dy+z\\,dz,$ where $C$ is a portion of the helix $r(t)=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+t\\,k$ for $t\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{3}]?$" :question/worked-solution "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y(t)=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,z(t)=t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,k \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}-y\\,dx+x\\,dy+z\\,dz & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}-y\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+z\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}(-y\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+z\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot (-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot (\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)+t\\cdot 1\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}t+2{sin}^{2}⁡t+2{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}t+2\\,dt\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534981 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179729 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b5ecc45-95ec-55c0-86bf-bbaeffef4049" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Sum of Line Integrals With Respect to X, Y, and Z"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08b00f42-9741-5f92-9339-a2a2a3e0a478" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }5\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+{e}^{t}\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534275} {:answer/id #uuid "236555c7-ee6e-5be6-bd74-3a41e1426296" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }25\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t+{e}^{t}\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534341} {:answer/id #uuid "443fcd61-e7db-54c9-9474-4eaf8ee080b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }5\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t+{e}^{2t}\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534394} {:answer/id #uuid "69837eb7-597e-5314-9105-3e7be9be3024" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }25\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+{e}^{2t}\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534482} {:answer/id #uuid "788fc73e-f6c0-5d4e-9563-fec8ac0a5b5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{e}^{2t}\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534521}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69837eb7-597e-5314-9105-3e7be9be3024" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }25\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+{e}^{2t}\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534482} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f0f87ed-2e6a-5c16-a67c-0ec64db6f138" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534921}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "198d2d03-309c-5424-a889-3994cff0e1c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-124837" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}y\\,dx+x\\,dy+z\\,dz,$ where $C$ is a portion of the curve $r(t)=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+{e}^{t}\\,k$ for $t\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ]?$" :question/worked-solution "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y(t)=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,z(t)={e}^{t}.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})\\,k \\\\  & =-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+{e}^{t}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}y\\,dx+x\\,dy+z\\,dz & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }y\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+z\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(y\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+z\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot (-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot (5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)+{e}^{t}\\cdot {e}^{t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }25{cos}^{2}⁡t-25{sin}^{2}⁡t+{e}^{2t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }25\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+{e}^{2t}\\,dt\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535072 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179729 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b5ecc45-95ec-55c0-86bf-bbaeffef4049" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Sum of Line Integrals With Respect to X, Y, and Z"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ef8374b-3c52-5aba-a47f-1d45b49a355d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{2}^{3}5{t}^{2}+25t\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534297} {:answer/id #uuid "6884847b-94e5-5d69-9c17-87b636deade0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{2}^{3}{t}^{4}-4\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534478} {:answer/id #uuid "e072df42-f8fc-5db8-a2ff-18aa9b23b0c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{2}^{3}3{t}^{2}+13\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534764} {:answer/id #uuid "f416e42b-335d-5fe1-b1a3-8afe51f7521e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{2}^{3}{t}^{3}+20t\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534809} {:answer/id #uuid "f5c66fb6-5b2d-57cc-b4d1-6389f608194b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{2}^{3}t+12\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534812}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ef8374b-3c52-5aba-a47f-1d45b49a355d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{2}^{3}5{t}^{2}+25t\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534297} :answer-field/id #uuid "b181f285-5443-572d-9a9e-98fe01481860" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534933}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d6062a1b-c189-5825-831a-1185f156e120" :question/math-academy-id "q-124866" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}xy\\,dx+yz\\,dy+z\\,dz,$ where $C$ is a portion of the line $r(t)=t\\,i+5t\\,j+\\,k$ for $t\\in [2,3]?$" :question/worked-solution "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=t,\\,y(t)=5t,\\,z(t)=1.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)\\,k \\\\  & =\\,i+5\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}xy\\,dx+yz\\,dy+z\\,dz & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}xy\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+yz\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+z\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}(xy\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+yz\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+z\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}5{t}^{2}\\cdot (1)+5t\\cdot (5)+1\\cdot (0)\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}5{t}^{2}+25t\\,dt\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535023 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179675 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3be2c44e-775f-53fa-a078-cff25eaea903" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Sum of Line Integrals With Respect to X and Y"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22201dff-61e9-5435-a6a4-ec1001f8fba7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534336} {:answer/id #uuid "968eea0b-a6c3-5719-af51-829806f3263f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)-{cos}^{2}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534597} {:answer/id #uuid "9e5e15da-7973-535e-a572-2e011cbd5da9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534619} {:answer/id #uuid "c3d52a07-3bbb-53b0-a0b0-9e85a23a30bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)-1\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534703} {:answer/id #uuid "efcdd02b-1a12-5093-8ddd-b0ba2d89d81e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534799}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22201dff-61e9-5435-a6a4-ec1001f8fba7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534336} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0258956-1ae0-545c-833f-e715647fb6c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534947}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6f3c55a9-3e7c-5106-8273-98cee0c05243" :question/math-academy-id "q-124870" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}x\\,dx+({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,dy,$ where $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\,i+j$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ]?$" :question/worked-solution "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t),\\,y(t)=1.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)\\,j \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,i.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}x\\,dx+({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+({sin}^{2}⁡(2t)-{1}^{2})\\cdot 0\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387595 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179675 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3be2c44e-775f-53fa-a078-cff25eaea903" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Sum of Line Integrals With Respect to X and Y"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0ab06e7-79ee-52e5-97b8-b09ca19ff9d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{2}4{t}^{3}-2\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387597} {:answer/id #uuid "17865438-efe9-5b9c-b46b-69626801cb2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{2}4{t}^{3}-t-2\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387598} {:answer/id #uuid "58c65698-3ae2-5632-8d41-3ea33a7f60d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{2}4{t}^{3}+t-2\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387599} {:answer/id #uuid "1aa73ede-da2c-528c-9ba2-3fad94a50974" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{2}t(4{t}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387600} {:answer/id #uuid "4451a1e7-6886-5ad0-87e2-9966e8fe1036" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{2}4{t}^{3}-3t-2\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387601}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17865438-efe9-5b9c-b46b-69626801cb2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{2}4{t}^{3}-t-2\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387598} :answer-field/id #uuid "172fec57-96a0-50f2-ac12-0a3d7d9d4085" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387596}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "87d7259c-ca26-53c7-b47d-c8aa49f4ead9" :question/math-academy-id "q-124875" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}(x+y)\\,dx+(x+2)\\,dy,$ where $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=(t-2)\\,i+({t}^{3}-t)\\,j$ for $t\\in [1,2]?$" :question/worked-solution "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=t-2,\\,y(t)={t}^{3}-t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-2)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-t)\\,j \\\\  & =i+(3{t}^{2}-1)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}(x+y)\\,dx+(x+2)\\,dy & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(x+y)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+(x+2)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}((x+y)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+(x+2)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(t-2+{t}^{3}-t)\\cdot 1+(t-2+2)\\cdot (3{t}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{t}^{3}-2+3{t}^{3}-t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}4{t}^{3}-t-2\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534996 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179675 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3be2c44e-775f-53fa-a078-cff25eaea903" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Sum of Line Integrals With Respect to X and Y"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04a0d4eb-fefb-5e1d-8b8b-53d270e9ff12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534270} {:answer/id #uuid "29ed2488-96ec-539f-848b-3a7f0c77834e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534351} {:answer/id #uuid "5642d196-fd16-5650-b8ce-2b73794cc067" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534439} {:answer/id #uuid "6afc72d8-8408-50d9-bca7-f953e40f36f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534485} {:answer/id #uuid "bae2108b-9562-5fdc-b2ed-c916f2046fc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534683}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6afc72d8-8408-50d9-bca7-f953e40f36f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534485} :answer-field/id #uuid "15565180-33b3-52ce-9a0a-037fbe40360a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534841}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "34262fe5-7916-5312-b653-79d60bb7bbe7" :question/math-academy-id "q-124877" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}y\\,dx+x\\,dy,$ where $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,\\pi ]?$" :question/worked-solution "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}y\\,dx+x\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }y\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }-{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387602 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179675 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3be2c44e-775f-53fa-a078-cff25eaea903" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Sum of Line Integrals With Respect to X and Y"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b918e4b-1a1e-5f07-bdcf-0df01823351b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387604} {:answer/id #uuid "a77ab89f-7ff2-56aa-92f3-8a34cf546faa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387605} {:answer/id #uuid "64a45e8f-6b03-5181-98e0-7fde3fd7fe3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387606} {:answer/id #uuid "6ee9fd46-5e14-597a-ac4f-5e151b3f61d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387607} {:answer/id #uuid "224a08b6-da5a-55cd-9556-62aee27206f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387608}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a77ab89f-7ff2-56aa-92f3-8a34cf546faa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387605} :answer-field/id #uuid "01902e7a-397e-5cde-855b-33f1e55a1d2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387603}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a6c4d7e0-6d3a-5784-88f9-be750756f8cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-124878" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}(x-y)\\,dx+(y-x)\\,dy,$ where $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]?$" :question/worked-solution "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,y(t)=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}(x-y)\\,dx+(y-x)\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(x-y)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+(y-x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}((x-y)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+(y-x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t))\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+4{cos}^{2}⁡t-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-4{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}4({cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259748 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179675 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3be2c44e-775f-53fa-a078-cff25eaea903" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Sum of Line Integrals With Respect to X and Y"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e2f5a62-76c0-5bdc-a396-495124af352b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{{t}^{2}+1}{t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257340} {:answer/id #uuid "5a097155-4e1b-5b9c-a7d7-50cdbc47a65d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257563} {:answer/id #uuid "96907a59-7d6a-527c-98d4-1e35892835f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{3}2t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258111} {:answer/id #uuid "be181f17-69a9-5b4f-8f75-9f9327f69a8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{{t}^{2}-1}{t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258440} {:answer/id #uuid "d3b7af4e-c8d9-5619-8114-bcd7561b76af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{t-1}{t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258636}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be181f17-69a9-5b4f-8f75-9f9327f69a8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{{t}^{2}-1}{t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258440} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa0f63c4-0bd4-586a-ba7e-dc23082dd8ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259472}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b4c0124c-a7c2-5baf-8b6a-e564a05c4df8" :question/math-academy-id "q-124885" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}x{y}^{2}\\,dx+\\frac{1}{x}\\,dy,$ where $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+t\\,j$ for $t\\in [1,3]?$" :question/worked-solution "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\frac{1}{t},\\,y(t)=t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,j \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,i+j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}x{y}^{2}\\,dx+\\frac{1}{x}\\,dy & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}x{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+\\frac{1}{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(x{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{1}{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{t}\\cdot {t}^{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}})+\\frac{1}{(\\frac{1}{t})}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}-\\frac{1}{t}+t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{{t}^{2}-1}{t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180285 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179734 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2daf57e1-a02d-5e5f-b4a4-bb8ae9638a75" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Line Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de4f1230-67f0-5878-83fe-a6933cc0143a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179255} {:answer/id #uuid "f0d7b0f8-c3f8-570a-be6c-1090a467157a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179256} {:answer/id #uuid "4d94b4e5-2834-504a-bdd8-957d26c3eb45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179257} {:answer/id #uuid "4f2d9a41-f005-55e4-861b-e7cf0046c31a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179258} {:answer/id #uuid "6128b4a2-642c-5954-a078-3678e17ec99b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179259}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f2d9a41-f005-55e4-861b-e7cf0046c31a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179258} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd768c8b-7e94-5271-a295-67cfb51c0e42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179254}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7db959c5-fcb6-5723-b0e1-39e452e905f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-81170" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}\\frac{x}{y}\\,dx+\\frac{y}{x}\\,dy,$ where $C$ is a portion of the ellipse $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$" :question/worked-solution "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y(t)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\frac{x}{y}\\,dx+\\frac{y}{x}\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{x}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+\\frac{y}{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(\\frac{x}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{y}{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\cdot (2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,dt \\\\  & ={-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[-\\frac{1}{2}-0]-[0-4] \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413042 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179734 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2daf57e1-a02d-5e5f-b4a4-bb8ae9638a75" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Line Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ea3a4f2-a959-540f-86d2-a526fb567a9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413009} {:answer/id #uuid "6cf6010e-a80e-5fc9-aa97-fc8be288477c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413015} {:answer/id #uuid "7acff49a-3d77-5139-87b8-23f8a83a61d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413018} {:answer/id #uuid "874aecd7-c4bb-5970-a264-ff44eec6444f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413020} {:answer/id #uuid "d33fa25d-bc45-54e8-8056-40b5e874ab27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413032}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "874aecd7-c4bb-5970-a264-ff44eec6444f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413020} :answer-field/id #uuid "516d65af-e99b-58a7-afb3-db833a18796f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413038}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7e1c746b-98be-5a3b-93f3-3c945fad75be" :question/math-academy-id "q-90723" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}(3x+y)\\,dx+x\\,dy,$ where $C$ is a portion of the parabola parametrized by $r(t)={t}^{2}\\,i+(4t-1)\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2].$" :question/worked-solution "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)={t}^{2},\\,y(t)=4t-1.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-1)\\,j \\\\  & =2t\\,i+4\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can calculate the line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}(3x+y)\\,dx+x\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(3x+y)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}((3x+y)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(3{t}^{2}+4t-1)\\cdot 2t+{t}^{2}\\cdot 4\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}6{t}^{3}+8{t}^{2}-2t+4{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}6{t}^{3}+12{t}^{2}-2t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{4}+4{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{3}{2}(2)^{4}+4(2)^{3}-{2}^{2}]-[0] \\\\  & =[24+32-4] \\\\  & =52\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535057 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179734 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2daf57e1-a02d-5e5f-b4a4-bb8ae9638a75" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Line Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "207d4a62-e83c-5373-b357-2c60fca0d97f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534330} {:answer/id #uuid "3a8cdc89-1beb-5512-8aa9-412f93b2dc69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{18}(4-\\pi )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534377} {:answer/id #uuid "49708f11-fe31-57c8-a150-b389b458ddef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534405} {:answer/id #uuid "8110d653-b1b2-5b3d-ad4c-5d3fcbdf4a28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534544} {:answer/id #uuid "9ccd828c-0bdc-55ab-900f-109f767fab40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}(9-\\pi )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534615}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ccd828c-0bdc-55ab-900f-109f767fab40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}(9-\\pi )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534615} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a2b773f-820b-5bd4-95ab-10a27879c738" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534898}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b34fc554-6133-5c96-98c9-93a11d4b7862" :question/math-academy-id "q-90834" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}-y\\,dx+x\\,dy-z\\,dz,$ where $C$ is a portion of the helix parametrized by $r(t)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+2t\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$" :question/worked-solution "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y(t)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,z(t)=2t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,k \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+2k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate the line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}-y\\,dx+x\\,dy-z\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}-y\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt-z\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(-y\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}-z\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot (-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot (3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-2t\\cdot 2\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}9{sin}^{2}⁡t+9{cos}^{2}⁡t-4t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}9-4t\\,dt \\\\  & =(9t-2{t}^{2}){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{2}-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}(9-\\pi )\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534974 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179734 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2daf57e1-a02d-5e5f-b4a4-bb8ae9638a75" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Line Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54af8bf2-64e5-57dd-8bdc-cc8a15802ee4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(\\pi +1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534434} {:answer/id #uuid "7fd34733-2faf-5ece-8584-4e5eca4bc119" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi +2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534541} {:answer/id #uuid "a7d34679-3dab-5b88-b269-717361d9312e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534640} {:answer/id #uuid "e00ce6fd-a2c8-597a-a47a-948b2ab26963" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534763} {:answer/id #uuid "f278dfee-2cf0-5ffd-b38d-93d20e6a0a87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(\\pi -1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534803}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54af8bf2-64e5-57dd-8bdc-cc8a15802ee4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(\\pi +1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534434} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5b05707-d90c-5874-90a1-dd42c5f8c325" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534950}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "08e87b9c-9adc-5a8c-b060-dda37adbb915" :question/math-academy-id "q-90840" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}-\\frac{1}{y}\\,dx+\\frac{y}{x}\\,dy+dz,$ where $C$ is a portion of the helix parametrized by $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+t\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,\\pi ].$" :question/worked-solution "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,z(t)=t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,k \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can calculate the line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}-\\frac{1}{y}\\,dx+\\frac{y}{x}\\,dy+dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }-\\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+\\frac{y}{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(-\\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{y}{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)+1\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(2t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(2\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡0 \\\\  & =2(\\pi +1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
